From eb3cd728751cc2fd88bb565ed1c6492a70944ed8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:17:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 128/294] gallium/pvr: write the firmware's static programs
 into the carveouts

The GPU expects certain programs to already be sitting at fixed addresses inside the
carveouts before a context can exist: a VDM sync program and the pixel-event/EOT
program. They are now placed, verified on the real kernel:

  pvr: static memory: 12 bytes of firmware programs in 3 carveouts
  vm: firmware programs: VDM sync verified at the kernel's USC vdm_sync offset,
      PDS launcher and pixel-event programs generated

Both halves of the VDM sync are needed and both are produced: the USC code is copied from
pco's precompiled library (16 bytes of NOP common program, small by design) and the PDS
program that launches it is generated by libpowervr_pds with pvr_pds_setup_doutu pointing
at where the USC code was just written. The pixel-event program comes from
pvr_pds_generate_pixel_event.

The check is shaped around what actually matters here. It is not enough that bytes were
written - a firmware program at the wrong offset is EXECUTED as something else entirely -
so the USC carveout is compared byte-for-byte against the source binary at the kernel's
own vdm_sync offset. That tests the placement, not just the write. The two generated
programs are checked for being non-empty rather than compared, because a generator that
silently produced nothing would otherwise look like success.

Corrections found while writing it, all mine:

* pvr_pds_generate_pixel_event's fourth argument is the device info, not a size
  out-parameter; its return value is where the next constant would go, so the program's
  size is the distance from where it was written. The header's macros hide this.
* libpowervr_pds_includes is an IncludeDirs, so it belongs in include_directories and not
  in dependencies - meson rejects it with a clear message.
* The reported 12 bytes deliberately counts only what was copied. The generated programs'
  sizes are not tracked, and the check says so rather than implying the total is the
  firmware's full footprint.

Still no job submission: these programs sit in memory and nothing executes them yet.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/meson.build  |  10 +-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_probe.c  |  75 ++++++++++-
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_static.c | 189 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_static.h |  42 ++++++
 4 files changed, 311 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_static.c
 create mode 100644 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_static.h

